📅 Day 54 – Session Management (Cookies & HttpSession)

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session focused on session management in web applications using Cookies and HttpSession. The mentor explained how web applications maintain user data across multiple requests, since HTTP is a stateless protocol.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ Session Management
HTTP is a stateless protocol (no memory of previous requests)
Session management is used to track user data across multiple requests
2️⃣ Cookies
Stored on the client-side (browser)
Used to store small pieces of data
Sent with every request to the server
🔹 Key Methods:
addCookie()
getCookies()
3️⃣ HttpSession
Stored on the server-side
Used to maintain user session data
More secure compared to cookies
🔹 Key Methods:
setAttribute()
getAttribute()
invalidate()
🔹 Practical Work

During the practice session, I:

Created programs to store user data using cookies
Retrieved cookie data from browser
Used HttpSession to store and manage user information
Tested session tracking across multiple requests

This helped me understand how session tracking works in real-time web applications.